rule: ELIM-G-5, CORE-INV-9
countdown returns IO (); raised, it takes the world and returns IORes, and
calls itself with the next world.
CHECK: -- specialization of Main.countdown(_:Int) .PrimIO.MkIO#0 @(_:%World)
CHECK-NEXT: Main.countdown#[[C:[0-9]+]] (%{{[0-9]+}} : w Int) (%{{[0-9]+}} : 1 %World) : PrimIO.IORes[Builtin.Unit] =
CHECK-NEXT: case %{{[0-9]+}} of
CHECK: = Main.countdown#[[C]](%{{[0-9]+}}, %{{[0-9]+}})
CHECK: -- specialization of Main.main() .PrimIO.MkIO#0 @(_:%World)
CHECK: = Main.countdown#[[C]](%{{[0-9]+}}, %{{[0-9]+}})
